                          <msItem>                            
                            <textLang mainLang="pgl-Ogam">Primitive Irish written in ogham script</textLang>                            
                           </msItem>
                    </msContents>
                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support><p><ref target="https://www.archaeology.ie/archaeological-survey-ireland/historic-environment-viewer-application">National Monuments Service</ref> SMR ID: <idno type="SMR">WA003-030----</idno></p> 
                                    <material type="stone">Old red sandstone</material> 
                                    <objectType key="monument">Pillar</objectType> 
                                    <dimensions unit="m" source="MOO1999">
                                            <height>2.00</height>
                                            <width>0.75</width>
                                            <depth>0.40</depth>
                                       </dimensions>
                                </support>
                                <condition>Probably erected as a standing stone with a rectangular cross-section oriented N-S (Moore 1999, no. 1485). This irregularly-shaped monolith is worn and damaged. Macalister (1949, 293) suggested that <q>the inscribed face is recessed by violent hammering to a depth of about 7 ins. behind its original surface, almost certainly to remove an earlier inscription</q>.</condition>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout style="vertical" rend="arris_upR-upL">The inscription reads upwards on two angles (SE and SW). As noted by Macalister (1945, 293) the inscription appears to begin on the right or sinister angle. He comments that this is <q>remarkably frequent in this part of the country</q>.</layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote>The inscription appears to have been <rs type="execution"  key="pocked" ref="https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/11.html">pocked</rs> and rubbed. The ogham strokes are bold and quite evenly spaced. <height></height>
                            </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                    </physDesc>
