        <body>
           <div type="edition" subtype="ogham" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="pgl" resp="#NW">
            <ab>
                    <lb n="1" style="text-direction:up"/><persName><name nymRef="#vocagnas">ᚃᚑᚉᚐᚌᚅᚔ</name> 
                    <lb n="2" style="text-direction:up"/><w type="formula" lemma="maqqas">ᚋᚐᚊᚔ</w> <name nymRef="#curitas?">ᚉᚒᚏ<supplied reason="lost">ᚔ</supplied>ᚈ</name></persName>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="edition" subtype="transliteration" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="pgl" resp="#NW">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1" style="text-direction:up"/><persName><name nymRef="#vocagnas">VOCAGNI</name> 
                    <lb n="2" style="text-direction:up"/><w type="formula" lemma="maqqas">MAQI</w> <name nymRef="#curitas?">CUR<supplied reason="lost">I</supplied>T</name></persName>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                <app n="1">   
                    <note>Macalister (1945, 293) noted that the strokes of the second name are faint, especially those of
3I (here supplied as no longer evident) and that the top of the stone is broken, possibly resuting in the loss of a vowel in the father's name (CUR[I]T[I]).</note>
                </app>
                </listApp>
            </div>
            <div type="translation">
                <p>of Fochán (*Vocagnas) son of Curid (? *Curitas?)</p>
            </div>
